<ul>
<li>To get the cell above it (<code>dp[r-1][c]</code>), we only need access=
 to the previous row.</li>
<li>To get the cell to its left (<code>dp[r][c-1]</code>), we just need to =
look at the cell to the left of the current cell, which is in the same row =
we're currently populating.</li>
</ul>
<p>Therefore, we only need to maintain two rows:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>prev_row</code>: the previous row.</li>
<li><code>curr_row</code>: the current row being populated.</li>
</ul>
